// Targets a creature you TOUCH ("cast on self or an ally by touch" per the
// sheet's own notes), not the caster unconditionally -- `SelfBuff` always
// lands its effect on the caster (`entity: data.entity` in
// `common/src/states/self_buff.rs`), never a touched ally, so this uses
// `BasicMelee` with the established touch-ally pattern (spare_the_dying.ron
// in this same folder; weave_transfusion.ron / lesser_restoration.ron /
// greater_restoration.ron in transmutation/abjuration): a near-inert Stab
// whose `attack_effect_target: InGroup` redirects the effect onto whoever is
// struck instead of dealing damage.
//
// Every existing InGroup precedent delivers `Heal` or `RemoveBuff` via
// `attack_effect`; this is the first to deliver a plain `CombatEffect::Buff`
// that way. Same resolution code path (`combat.rs`'s `CombatEffect::Buff`
// arm reads whatever `target` the attack resolved against, `InGroup` or
// not), so no new mechanism -- just the first RON to combine two
// already-real pieces. Flagging for reviewer attention per plan §5 item 1.
//
// Grants `Shielded` (temp-HP absorb pool -- see false_life.ron's own use of
// this buff) on the touched ally, modeling "steadying it against the brink
// of death". The retaliatory-necrotic-lash-on-attacker rider is dropped: no
// `BuffKind` models a reactive damage-the-attacker-on-being-hit effect
// (checked every variant in `common/src/comp/buff.rs`), the same class of
// gap chill_touch.ron's own header already documents for this school.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 45.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Buff((
                kind: Shielded,
                dur_secs: 60.0,
                strength: Value(25.0),
                chance: 1.0,
            )),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Necromancy), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
